# Model & Enum

## Model (matches user.go)

```go
package model

import (
    "go-skeleton/internal/model/enum"
    "time"
)

func (User) TableName() string { return "user" }

type UserStatus = enum.UserStatus

type User struct {
    ID     string     `gorm:"primarykey;default:gen_random_uuid()"`
    Status UserStatus `gorm:"column:status"`
}
```

## Enum (matches enum/generic_status.go)

```go
package enum

type GenericStatus int64

const (
    ACTIVE GenericStatus = iota + 1
    INACTIVE
)

var genericStatusKey = map[GenericStatus]string{
    ACTIVE: "active", INACTIVE: "inactive",
}

func (s GenericStatus) String() string { return genericStatusKey[s] }

func (s *GenericStatus) Scan(value interface{}) error { /* string → enum */ }
```

## Do / Don't

- DO: type alias on model (`type X = enum.X`)
- DON'T: inline string/const enums on model files
